// The inverse of `hhmmToMinutes`: a minute-of-day as its "HH:MM" wall-clock string, zero-padded and 24-hour.
//
// NORMALIZED MODULO THE DAY, which is the whole reason this is one function. The same arithmetic had been spelled six ways in allos
// and three of them disagreed off the end of the day: an hour mapped to minutes (1440 -> "00:00") and a wall-clock end that ran past
// midnight both need the wrap, while a naive `Math.floor(m / 60)` with `padStart` answers "24:00" and a naive `%` keeps JS's sign and
// answers "-1:-30" for -30. Both of those are wrong at every call site, so neither is reachable from here.
//
